<title>UK: Woolwich says no immediate plans on rates.</title>
<headline>Woolwich says no immediate plans on rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Woolwich Building Society said on Friday it had no immediate plans to make a move on lending rates after the Bank of England said raised official interest rates to 6.5 percent from 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We are watching and waiting. We are always reviewing but not reviewing specifically in reaction to (today's) interest rate change,&quot; a spokesman said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
